From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:46:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rust: soc: apple: rtkit: Lend out the C handle

The AOP's firmware-driven suspend calls RTKit's AP power notices, which
have no Rust wrapper, through the C handle. Aurora added this accessor
with an unrelated platform series that this tree doesn't carry; add it
alone, with the same text.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 rust/kernel/soc/apple/rtkit.rs | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rust/kernel/soc/apple/rtkit.rs b/rust/kernel/soc/apple/rtkit.rs
index 9d92b73ffa..6f4c3c1b7f 100644
--- a/rust/kernel/soc/apple/rtkit.rs
+++ b/rust/kernel/soc/apple/rtkit.rs
@@ -369,6 +369,12 @@ impl<T: Operations> RtKit<T> {
         })
     }
 
+    /// Borrows the C handle without transferring ownership.
+    /// The owner must outlive each unsafe C operation and its callbacks.
+    pub fn as_raw(&self) -> *mut bindings::apple_rtkit {
+        self.rtk
+    }
+
     /// Returns whether the coprocessor is running (not crashed, IOP and AP power states on).
     pub fn is_running(&self) -> bool {
         // SAFETY: `rtk` is valid per the type invariant. The call only reads state.
